diff --git a/src/backend/fixtures/knownBugs/README.md b/src/backend/fixtures/knownBugs/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9cb098f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/backend/fixtures/knownBugs/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+# Known Phoenix bugs
+
+`known-bugs.json` lists regression cases that fail because of a confirmed bug in Phoenix, not because of the test. The `knownBug` fixture in `baseFixture.ts` reads it after every test.
+
+## What a listed case does
+
+| The case on a listed environment | Result in the report |
+|----------------------------------|----------------------|
+| Fails or times out, and the error matches `errorPattern` | Not counted as failed. Labelled `known-bug` with the Jira key. Counted under "known bugs" in Slack. Its REG ticket stays Failed. |
+| Fails with a different error | Failed, labelled `known-bug-drift`. Something new is wrong. |
+| Passes | Failed, labelled `known-bug-fixed`. The bug no longer reproduces, so remove the entry. |
+| Runs on an environment that is not listed | Judged normally. |
+
+In the HTML report, type `annot:known-bug` in the search box to list them.
+
+## Entry
+
+```json
+{
+  "case": "REG-1008",
+  "jira": "PHN-1234",
+  "envs": ["dev", "test"],
+  "errorPattern": "No invoices found",
+  "summary": "Billing run creates no invoice for a scale with scale code",
+  "markedOn": "2026-11-18"
+}
+```
+
+| Field | Meaning |
+|-------|---------|
+| `case` | The id in the test title, for example `REG-1008`. For a test with no id, use `title` with the exact test title instead. |
+| `jira` | Key of the Phoenix bug ticket. `null` only while the ticket is being created. |
+| `envs` | Environments where the bug is confirmed: `dev`, `dev2`, `test`. |
+| `errorPattern` | Regular expression, case-insensitive, matched against the error text of the failure. Keep it as specific as the error allows. |
+| `summary` | One line that says what is wrong in Phoenix. |
+| `markedOn` | Date the entry was added. |
+
+Add an entry only after the failure is confirmed as a Phoenix bug. Remove it when the bug is fixed on that environment.
